Unsupervised learning:
It is the process of finding the insights or pattern grouping of data set.
It is the process of working only with independent variable or x data

Types of Unsupervised learning
1.K-means clustering(grouping)
   K-Means clustering = a way to group similar things together, when we don’t know the group names in advance.
   eg:
   Imagine you have a garden with different flowers.
   You don’t know their names.
   But you measure things like height, petal size, and color shade.
   Here K=3
  Cluster 1 → Small red flowers
  Cluster 2 → Tall yellow flowers
  Cluster 3 → Medium white flowers

Now you want to group similar flowers together without knowing their labels.
